Rogue Class is a toy Linux distribution for playing games and reading
books. Rogue Class has a streamlined installer and it supports joystick
controls in most of the programs. RCL favors turn-based games, such as
puzzles and rogue-like games. Rogue Class is based heavily on Slackware
Linux. The scripting language is TCL. The graphical interface is Agar,
running on SDL and the Linux VESA framebuffer.  Version 4 adds support
for installing to USB flash media, reading EPUB files, and includes 3
new games: Brogue, Gruesome, and the tiles version of Dungeon Crawl
Stone Soup. To download RCL, visit rogueclass.org

